  "plan64Findings": [
    "Only the existing finite Claude checkpoint selects the helper. Codex/OpenCode do not enter it; no genuine vendor command, runtime mode or production authority is introduced.",
    "One checkpoints.read after both warm Stops and before first.close checks original member/source generation, exact checkpoint id/reference and owner-eligible/native-backing-unverified. It adds no capture and does not claim that owner eligibility proves native backing.",
    "The moved Restore block preserves old session continuity, changed generation within the same run, zero replay allocation/input, current sourceB, one continuation and closed/released Stop. The independent text inverse closes the whole moved block under explicit parameter and equivalent string-assertion substitutions.",
    "After restored Stop, one fresh Launch uses the original roster/capture/start/readiness path on cold epoch/teamA/currentB with B-fresh keys. It requires a distinct launch id/capability, precisely one appended Job, one current-peer initialized event with restored=false, and a distinct nonempty session. The unchanged jobEntry uses scoped entry bounds and original root/witness.",
    "Before one fresh boot the entire native input ledger is unchanged. After successful original terminal polling exactly one row is added, its old prefix remains exact, and pid/session/marker/native UUID are checked. Runtime delivery ids are checked separately from native UUIDs, and unrelated generations across fresh runs are not equated.",
    "The explicit fresh Stop must return closed/released. Helper result fields do not replace physical proof: original epoch close, pre-wait resumed/Stop/drain/release snapshot, original HANDLE wait, sentinel/source-pin checks and error aggregation remain exact.",
    "Helper interface is limited to existing RPC/data/observers and bound boot/launch callbacks; Job dependency is type-only. No runtime cycle, owner registry, timer, retry loop or native protocol is added.",
    "Original15-second action/poll bounds,25ms cadence and120-second outer controller remain. The extra read/launch/input/Stop have real cost and must fit the existing original CI budget. Static review neither predicts a pass nor grants an extension."
  ],
  "plan66Findings": [
    "Only min-h-8 is added to the existing inner assignee slot. canReassign/onOwnerChange, all picker/badge/unassigned props, callbacks and owner/read-only/call-time guards remain exact.",
    "The local minimum-height reservation addresses the source-confirmed presentation height difference without hiding refresh or preserving stale authority. Larger/wrapped content can grow. No universal viewport stability or exact historical owner-transition cause is asserted.",
    "Header is appended after all256 common source pins, including prior CDP. The separate27/46 arrays and all other text are unchanged. No UI helper, selector, action, stability sample, coordinate tolerance, timeout or cleanup change is included.",
    "Independent Plan65 remains preserved in later bf6/currentb60. Its stronger clarification-read expression and this height reservation address separate properties. The original failed Taskboard result is not promoted; original strict resulting-source acceptance remains."
  ],
